00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:55.000
Good morning and welcome to City Football Club.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:01.000
I'd like to give you some useful information about your visit to the stadium today

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:07.000
and then we'll start the tour of the areas of the stadium that are open to visitors.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:15.000
I can see lots of children here today, so just to let mums and dads know a few things before we start.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:20.000
The stadium has lots of stairs and the players' tunnel is very dark.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:25.000
Please don't let your children wander off on their own, even for a minute.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:29.000
We don't want any accidents or anyone getting frightened.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:37.000
Cameras are permitted everywhere and you can take pictures of your child shooting a penalty.

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:43.000
Assistants are helping to organise this and hopefully the queue won't be too long.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:47.000
It's very hot and sunny out on the pitch today.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:55.000
You can get food and drink at the cafe and I really recommend the healthy lunchboxes for children.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:02.000
Also in the cafe, children are invited to do a football-themed drawing.

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:06.000
We'll pick the best one at the end of the afternoon,

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:12.000
so don't forget to put your name and contact details on the back.

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:17.000
That way, if you've left the stadium before then, we'll send your prize,

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:20.000
but sadly we can't return drawings.

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:25.000
I'd like to mention some features of the tour.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:32.000
We'll start with the 360 cinema experience, which has been very popular over the years,

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:36.000
and then I'll take you to the players' dressing rooms,

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:41.000
before going outside to the seating area and the pitch.

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:46.000
I should say, if you'd prefer your visit to be self-guided,

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:50.000
please collect headphones from the reception,

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:55.000
and then you can listen to the pre-recorded information at your own speed.

00:02:56.000 --> 00:03:01.000
We've only just introduced this feature and would appreciate your feedback.

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:06.000
We're thinking of offering tours in other languages in future,

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:11.000
so if you have any thoughts on that, we'd welcome those too.

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:18.000
If you plan to return another time, you might like to book one of our VIP tours.

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:25.000
We've only just started offering these, and they can be booked online.

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:34.000
Before you hear the rest of the talk, you have some time to look at questions 15 to 20.

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:52.000
Now listen and answer questions 15 to 20.

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:55.000
Now listen and answer questions 15 to 20.

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:13.000
Now listen and answer questions 15 to 20.

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:19.000
Now, the stadium you see today was built in 1989,

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:23.000
as part of a three-year redevelopment project.

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:26.000
While that project was going on,

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:31.000
the team had to play its matches at the ground of another club.

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:37.000
Apart from that, the club has been here on this site since 1870.

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:42.000
As some of you may know, that was the start of a really important decade

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:46.000
in the history of football in this country.

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:53.000
For example, 1870 was also the year that football teams started to include

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:57.000
a player whose role it was to guard the goal.

00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:01.000
It's hard to imagine what the game must have been like

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:05.000
without someone in that position, isn't it?

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:12.000
In 1872 and 1873, many other clubs were established, both here and abroad.

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:16.000
And the following year, in 1874,

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:22.000
referees were allowed to send players off if they committed certain offences.

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:28.000
And also in that year, teams started having to swap ends at half-time.

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:32.000
One fact I was interested to discover

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:35.000
One fact I was interested to discover was

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:39.000
that in early football games, the aim was for the scorer

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:43.000
to get the ball between two flag posts

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:48.000
and later between sticks joined at the top with a piece of tape.

00:05:49.000 --> 00:05:54.000
In 1875, that tape was replaced with the solid crossbar

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:57.000
that we're familiar with today.

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:02.000
1877 saw the founding of further new clubs

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:06.000
and the history books tell us that in the same year

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:12.000
all the clubs decided to set a limit of 90 minutes for each match.

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:16.000
Before that, it was a more casual arrangement

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:20.000
and this sometimes caused huge arguments

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:23.000
and sometimes fights during matches

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:26.000
when one team called the end of the game

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:31.000
and the other team wanted to play on to try and score a winning goal.

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:38.000
By 1878, the number of teams in the football league increased again.

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:42.000
In addition, referees started using whistles

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:47.000
and electric lamps were installed on certain pitches.

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:50.000
This was a significant change

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:55.000
as games could then be played in the evenings all year round.

00:06:56.000 --> 00:07:01.000
In 1880, clubs began to charge fans for admission to games

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:07.000
even though players were still amateurs and had other proper jobs.

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:11.000
That's hard to imagine in the modern professional game

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:14.000
where top players earned significant sums of money

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:18.000
from both playing and commercial activities.

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:23.000
That is the end of Part 2.

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:28.000
You now have 30 seconds to check your answers to Part 2.

00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:52.000
Thank you for watching.

